CORE
continue_unconditional1.sv
--bound 2
^\[main\.0\.p0\] always main\.x == 3: PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.0\.p1\] always main\.y == \(main\.c \? 0 : 3\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.0\.p2\] always main\.c: REFUTED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
An unconditional continue (IEEE 1800-2017 12.8): the statements after it
are unreachable, and the path through the continue is the only path
that reaches the end of the loop body. After the loop, the path
condition is that on entry to the loop.
